   954	\section{Infinitely many triangles for curves of positive rank}\label{sec:triangles}
   955	We start by determining just one rational point on $\mathcal{E}_N$ that fulfills condition~(\ref{eq-13'}).
   956	This point will then be the stepping stone for an infinite number of such points.
   957	\begin{comment}
   958	\dc{Needed to start with something here? For example emphasizing the main result of the section or paper? Also, in the proofs of the lemmas in this section, the word
   959	``condition" has been used several times and we can remove some (?)}
   960	\end{comment}
   961	\begin{lem}\label{lem:1a}
   962	If $\mathcal{E}_N$ has positive rank for a rational number $N>1/4$, then there are rational points on $\mathcal{E}_N$ that satisfy condition~\eqref{eq-13'}.
   963	\end{lem}
   964	\begin{proof}
   965	Let $R=(u_R,v_R)$ be a rational non-torsion point on $\mathcal{E}_N$ that does not satisfy condition~\eqref{eq-13'}.
   966	If $u_R<1-4n$, then $R+T_3^-$ is a rational non-torison point satisfying condition~\eqref{eq-13'}.
   967	If $0<u_R<1$, then $-(R+T_6^-)$ is a rational non-torison point satisfying condition~\eqref{eq-13'}.
