  1150	\section{Poncelet's theorem}\label{sec:poncelet}
  1151	Our results now allow us to make an interesting statement with regard to Poncelet's closure theorem. 
  1152	\begin{comment}\dc{Reference?} 
  1153	\cb{Poncelet's Theorem is very well known.}
  1154	\end{comment}
  1155	\begin{cor}
  1156	Let $C$ and $E$ 
  1157	\begin{comment}
  1158	\dc{As suggested earlier, we may use the notations $C_r$ and $C_R$}
  1159	\cb{we keep $E$ and $C$.}
  1160	\end{comment} 
  1161	be two circles such that the ratio of their radii is rational and such that a triangle
  1162	with rational sides has  $C$ as circumcircle and  $E$ as one of its excircles. Then there exist infinitely
  1163	many rational non-similar triangles with rational sides that have  $C$ as circumcircle and  $E$ as excircle.
  1164	\end{cor}
