   888	and that these points lead to infinitely many non-similar integer triangles with $R/r=N$. 
   889	In this section we first show that for each $N=m^2\pm 1>1/4$, $m\in\Q$, the rank of $\mathcal{E}_N$ is positive.
   890	We provide explicit formulas for the sides $f,g,h$ of integer triangles with $R/r=N\in\Q$.   

