codex
The first construction-aware check exposed a genuine weakness at 96-bit sides: factoring the reduced numerator could reveal enough side factors. I raised the shipping regime to 256-bit sides; GNU’s standard factor utility then failed to finish a representative numerator within 15 seconds, while verification and the three-integer answer remain compact. I’m rerunning the stronger height-128 elliptic search across all seeds.
