A final suitability audit changed the disposition. The generic inverse family is locally hard, but recognizing the paper’s elliptic-curve change of variables still leaves the solver with the full rational-point search—there is no ≤300-operation compact route. Counting only the 18 verification operations would misreport G9(c). The paper’s closed-form \(N=m^2\pm1\) alternative also fails Track B: its measured mechanical method and compact route are the same 18-operation formula (about 13.6 µs at 256 bits), so there is no compression gap. I’m retaining the prototype and documenting an H/G9 rejection rather than shipping a misleading family.
