Rejected after full-paper and post-build audit.

- Generic inverse generation passes G and V, but Track A hardness is not established by the paper, and the elliptic-curve insight still leaves an unbounded search. The shipping instance required 12,639 failed point trials—over G9(c)’s 300-operation cap.
- The paper’s Theorem 4 construction also fails Track B: its mechanical solver and compact route are the same 18-operation formula, measured at roughly 13.6 μs per 256-bit instance. There is no compression gap.
- G1–G8 passed; G9 correctly records failure.
- OpenRouter returned HTTP 403 quota errors for every oracle call. These unscored transcripts were preserved but were not used as the rejection reason.

Files:

- [REJECTED.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2512.15237/REJECTED.md)
- [retained prototype](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2512.15237/rejected_gen_2512_15237.py)
- [selftest_report.json](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2512.15237/selftest_report.json)
- [README.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2512.15237/README.md)
- [bare oracle transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2512.15237/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [hinted transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2512.15237/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2512.15237/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

The source paper is available on [arXiv](https://arxiv.org/abs/2512.15237).
